WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.568
An estimated 98,000 Canadians dead by Medical Assistance in Dying.

00:00:04.568 --> 00:00:12.534
The confirmed count is 76,475 through December 2024 per Health Canada's corrected Sixth Annual Report.

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:16.806
16,499 killed in 2024 alone.

00:00:16.806 --> 00:00:19.988
5.1 percent of all Canadian deaths.

00:00:19.988 --> 00:00:23.193
Growth rate 6.9 percent year over year.

00:00:23.193 --> 00:00:29.352
At 45.2 deaths per day, approximately 21,000 more have died since the last report.

00:00:29.352 --> 00:00:31.636
One death every 32 minutes.

00:00:31.636 --> 00:00:35.011
The PM holds 6.8 million in Brookfield options.

00:00:35.011 --> 00:00:37.113
Brookfield owns seniors housing.

00:00:37.113 --> 00:00:38.829
The UN called for repeal.

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:40.931
10 provinces oppose expansion.

00:00:40.931 --> 00:00:43.602
Canada's response: no plans to act.

00:00:43.602 --> 00:00:46.499
State administered deaths have scaled aggressively.

00:00:46.499 --> 00:00:51.397
Five point one percent of all deaths in Canada — one in twenty — are now MAID.

00:00:51.397 --> 00:00:56.556
The government saves 20,685 dollars per death in palliative care avoided.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:01:01.874
The PM profits 69 dollars and 52 cents per dead Canadian through Brookfield options.

00:01:01.874 --> 00:01:05.852
102 doctors killed 373 people each.

00:01:05.852 --> 00:01:10.204
428 legal violations — zero referred to police.

00:01:10.204 --> 00:01:13.159
Track 2: Killing People Who Aren't Dying.

00:01:13.159 --> 00:01:17.772
732 non-terminal Canadians were killed by MAID in 2024.

00:01:17.772 --> 00:01:19.295
These people were not dying.

00:01:19.295 --> 00:01:26.465
They were killed because the government that expanded MAID failed to provide the housing, disability support, and mental health care that would have made it unnecessary.

00:01:26.465 --> 00:01:33.499
63 percent reported emotional distress or existential suffering, up from 35 percent in 2023.

00:01:33.499 --> 00:01:41.204
Poverty, housing insecurity, and mental illness are routinely documented as driving variables for Track 2 euthanasia expansion.

00:01:41.204 --> 00:01:48.863
In 2022, multiple veterans testified that government caseworkers offered them state-administered death instead of mobility ramps.

00:01:48.863 --> 00:01:53.704
Unlike European programs, Canada possesses zero independent oversight boards.

00:01:53.704 --> 00:02:02.215
Compliance is entirely self-reported by the physicians themselves, sparking condemnation from the United Nations Special Rapporteur on Human Rights.

00:02:02.215 --> 00:02:03.968
102 doctors.

00:02:03.968 --> 00:02:06.556
373 kills each.

00:02:06.556 --> 00:02:11.068
7 percent of MAID providers performed 38 percent of all deaths.

00:02:11.068 --> 00:02:18.613
At the estimated 100,000 total, these 102 doctors have personally killed approximately 38,000 Canadians.

00:02:18.613 --> 00:02:23.522
A peer-reviewed study called this policy capture by activists colonizing medicine.

00:02:23.522 --> 00:02:25.340
This is not a healthcare system.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:28.249
This is a kill chain operated by 102 people.

00:02:28.249 --> 00:02:30.284
The voices they tried to silence.

00:02:30.284 --> 00:02:35.443
Roger Foley reported hospital staff withheld food and water and suggested MAID four times.

00:02:35.443 --> 00:02:41.068
Heather Hancock was called selfish for declining MAID and told she was consuming resources.

00:02:41.068 --> 00:02:47.102
An 84-year-old Vancouver woman was offered MAID before diagnostic tests — she made a full recovery.

00:02:47.102 --> 00:02:48.647
These are not outliers.

00:02:48.647 --> 00:02:50.809
These are the system working as designed.

00:02:50.809 --> 00:02:55.806
Quebec has the highest MAID rate in the world at 67 deaths per 100,000.

00:02:55.806 --> 00:02:59.897
Three provinces account for 85 percent of all MAID deaths.

00:02:59.897 --> 00:03:01.045
Fiscal Motive.

00:03:01.045 --> 00:03:07.602
The Parliamentary Budget Officer calculated that expanding MAID would save the government 149 million dollars annually.

00:03:07.602 --> 00:03:14.806
A 2025 systemic analysis projected 1.273 trillion dollars in savings by 2047.

00:03:14.806 --> 00:03:19.874
The state is financially incentivized to end the lives of its most expensive citizens.

00:03:19.874 --> 00:03:25.886
The Parliamentary Budget Officer calculated that MAID saves the government 149 million dollars per year.

00:03:25.886 --> 00:03:28.943
They calculated this BEFORE Parliament voted to expand it.

00:03:28.943 --> 00:03:34.215
Projected savings: 1.273 trillion dollars by 2047.

00:03:34.215 --> 00:03:36.329
MAID is not just a medical program.

00:03:36.329 --> 00:03:39.079
It is fiscal policy disguised as compassion.

00:03:39.079 --> 00:03:41.090
What Accountability Looks Like.

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:43.568
We are not arguing about MAID's existence.

00:03:43.568 --> 00:03:45.977
The Supreme Court ruled it must exist.

00:03:45.977 --> 00:03:50.534
The accountability questions are: Why is there no independent oversight body?

00:03:50.534 --> 00:03:52.772
Why was the reflection period removed?

00:03:52.772 --> 00:03:55.784
Why are social support gaps driving MAID requests?

00:03:55.784 --> 00:03:58.522
Why has no Auditor General audit been conducted?

00:03:58.522 --> 00:04:03.727
Section 504 of the Criminal Code gives every Canadian the right to lay a private prosecution.

00:04:03.727 --> 00:04:05.295
Legislative Timeline.

00:04:05.295 --> 00:04:18.761
From the Carter v. Canada Supreme Court ruling in 2015, through Bill C-14 legalizing MAID in 2016, to Bill C-7's expansion in 2021 removing the requirement that death be reasonably foreseeable.

00:04:18.761 --> 00:04:28.147
Mental illness expansion has been delayed twice, now pushed to 2027 after opposition from psychiatrists, disability organizations, and UN human rights bodies.

00:04:28.147 --> 00:04:29.181
Sources.

00:04:29.234 --> 00:04:48.604
All data on this page comes from Health Canada's Annual Reports on MAID, Supreme Court and Quebec Superior Court rulings, Parliamentary bills C-14 and C-7, the Special Joint Committee on MAID, UN human rights reports, Veterans Ombudsman statements, and verified investigative journalism from CTV News and the Globe and Mail.

00:04:48.604 --> 00:04:51.365
Who Voted to Kill — The Parliamentary Record.

00:04:51.365 --> 00:04:57.752
76,475 Canadians confirmed dead because these MPs voted YEA.

00:04:57.752 --> 00:04:58.808
Two bills.

00:04:58.808 --> 00:04:59.888
Two votes.

00:04:59.888 --> 00:05:06.752
109 MPs voted for both C-14 and C-7, legalizing and then expanding MAID.

00:05:06.752 --> 00:05:10.831
173 total unique MPs across both votes.

00:05:10.831 --> 00:05:14.399
The largest state-administered killing program in the Western world.

00:05:14.399 --> 00:05:15.968
Provincial Pushback.

00:05:15.968 --> 00:05:22.593
10 provinces and territories signed a joint letter demanding an indefinite pause on MAID expansion to mental illness.

00:05:22.593 --> 00:05:28.706
Quebec refused — and has the highest MAID rate in the world at 7.9 percent of all deaths.

00:05:28.706 --> 00:05:36.127
Alberta introduced Bill 18 to limit MAID to Track 1 only, bar mental illness, and prohibit doctors from suggesting death.

00:05:36.127 --> 00:05:39.558
Manitoba denies MAID at 5 times the national average.

00:05:39.558 --> 00:05:46.843
The federal-provincial conflict is escalating: MAID eligibility is federal criminal law, but healthcare delivery is provincial.

00:05:46.843 --> 00:05:48.286
The law they are breaking.

00:05:48.286 --> 00:05:54.627
The Rome Statute — which Canada was the first country to implement — criminalises crimes against humanity.

00:05:54.627 --> 00:06:00.524
Article 7 defines this as a widespread or systematic attack directed against a civilian population.

00:06:00.524 --> 00:06:07.343
76,475 confirmed deaths directed by legislation is the definition of systematic.

00:06:07.343 --> 00:06:11.127
The Nuremberg Code requires voluntary consent without coercion.

00:06:11.127 --> 00:06:16.843
When a veteran calls asking for help and is offered death, that is coercion by deprivation.

00:06:16.843 --> 00:06:28.547
And in 1976, Canada abolished the death penalty for convicted murderers — then in 2016, it legalised the execution of the disabled, the elderly, the depressed, and the veteran, and called it compassion.

00:06:28.547 --> 00:06:30.002
The world is watching.

00:06:30.002 --> 00:06:33.729
The United Nations has called on Canada to repeal Track 2 entirely.

00:06:33.729 --> 00:06:36.456
Two Charter challenges are before the courts.

00:06:36.456 --> 00:06:41.888
Veterans testified that 20 of them have documented proof of being offered MAID when seeking healthcare.

00:06:41.888 --> 00:06:45.513
And the federal government says it has no plans to act on any of it.
